#!/usr/bin/python3
"""agos-firstboot: turn configuration inputs into a running agent desktop.

Runs as root from agos-firstboot.service on every boot, before the agent's
user manager (user@1000.service) starts. Implements docs/spec.md "First boot":

  1. merge config sources (defaults < AGOS filesystem < /etc/agos <
     systemd credentials), validate, write /run/agos/config.json
  2. generate missing secrets (AGENTD_TOKEN, VIEWER_PASSWORD when needed)
  3. render the KasmVNC display/users, agentd config + tokens, the agent's
     environment, the console banner and the Claude Code / T3 Code pre-seeds;
     enable or disable the T3 Code user unit
  4. join Tailscale and publish the viewer/agentd with `tailscale serve`
  5. write /var/lib/agos/state.json

`agos-firstboot --wait-ready` (agos-ready.service) waits for the desktop to
come up and flips state.json to "ready" (or "degraded").

Python 3 standard library only. Never prints secrets. Never fails the boot:
problems are recorded in state.json and the journal.
"""

